            <ArticleTitle>Delayed respiratory arrest after epidural hydromorphone.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>404-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case is reported where hydromorphone 1 mg injected into the epidural space produced apnoea 4.5 hours later. No other narcotics had been given in the previous 10 hours.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
